  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries independent predictive signal. Before investing the remaining 8 experiments in multimodal fusion configurations, I need a clean image-only baseline. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the image contribution using a standard encoder and the same singleprofile setting as the RNA baseline, so the comparison is controlled. If image-only substantially outperforms or underperforms RNA-only, it reshapes which modality to prioritize in multimodal fusion and whether a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) or learned RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt) is the higher-value next step. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the modality landscape with minimal confounding changes."
}

